      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-336639",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{\u2032}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${\u03a6}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{\u03a6}_{0}^{\u2032}(t)=A{\u03a6}_{0}(t),\\,{\u03a6}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${\u03a6}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={\u03a6}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,c$ \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $x({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0})=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ is true by {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by the fact that {{field-3}}."
